// The Reify feature tour. Recorded by `termgif record assets/demo.tg --terminal`.
//
// Screen-capture mode, not termgif's normal recorder, and that is the whole point:
// the normal recorder forces NO_COLOR=1 and TERM=dumb onto every command and reads
// its output through a pipe, so reify prints no colour at all. Screen-capture mode
// runs each command against a real terminal, so the status tags are coloured here
// exactly as a user sees them.
//
// Each command is prefixed with the prompt because screen-capture mode never draws
// one. `\u276f` is a real executable on PATH that execs its arguments, so the line both
// reads as a prompt and runs as the command.
//
// Every command runs for real against a real ERPNext index (~5,000 files, 15 years of
// history). Nothing is staged: if the GIF ever disagrees with the tool, re-record it.
//
// @theme, @size and @window-frame below are ignored in screen-capture mode - the look
// comes from the recording terminal, and assets/make-demo.py replaces its chrome.

@output "assets/demo.gif"
@title "reify"
@size 104x30
@font 15
@theme "dracula"
@fps 8
@speed 22ms
@colors 64
@lossy 90
@prompt "❯ "
@window-frame "minimal"
@cwd "."

~500ms

// Build the graph.
-> "❯ reify index" >>
~1600ms

// The flagship: the minimum context for a task, under a token budget.
-> "❯ reify context \"add a discount tier for strategic customers\" --budget 1500" >>
~2600ms

// Provenance for one line: callers, data, co-change, the commits that explain it.
-> "❯ reify why erpnext/selling/doctype/customer/customer.py:514" >>
~2600ms

// Blast radius, including hops no single grep would follow.
-> "❯ reify impact \"check_credit_limit\"" >>
~2200ms

// One business concept across every language, table and file it appears in.
-> "❯ reify explain \"credit limit\"" >>
~2200ms

// The agent-facing format: columns declared once, one row per record.
-> "❯ reify context \"block orders above the approval cap\" --budget 1200 --toon" >>
~2400ms
~1200ms
